    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1077">

                <pb facs="0792" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3793.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Simpich to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-24T18:00:00-07:23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At 8 o’clock last night committee Mexicans notified Americans in Nacozari they
                    must leave. Train was assembled, Americans were disarmed and placed aboard. All
                    arrived safely at Douglas on border 6 a.m. today. Estimated that hundred and
                    twenty Americans <pb facs="0793" n="677" xml:id="pg677"/> came out. Cananea
                    Consolidated Copper Company closing its mine at Cananea tonight. Second special
                    train being held there to bring out all remaining Americans who will come.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Simpich</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
